---
title: "delete_old_backups (Daily DB Backup Workflow)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_cutoff: CUTOFF = date -u -d 7 days ago +%Y-%m-%dT%H-%M-%SZ
    q_cutoff --> q_list: FILES = gh api repos/BACKUP_REPO/contents --jq .[].name
    q_list --> q_iter: iterate over FILES
    q_iter --> q_compare: for FILE in FILES
    q_compare --> q_delete: FILE < CUTOFF (lexicographic)
    q_compare --> q_iter: FILE >= CUTOFF (skip)
    q_iter --> [*]: all files processed
    q_delete --> q_get_sha: SHA = gh api repos/BACKUP_REPO/contents/FILE --jq .sha
    q_get_sha --> q_api_delete: gh api --method DELETE repos/BACKUP_REPO/contents/FILE --field message --field sha
    q_api_delete --> q_iter: deletion attempted (|| true ignores errors)

    note right of q_cutoff
        INV-001: retention window is exactly 7 days from current UTC time
        INV-002: CUTOFF format matches filename format for valid lexicographic comparison
    end note

    note right of q_compare
        INV-003: lexicographic comparison of ISO-8601 timestamps is equivalent to chronological ordering
        INV-004: files with names not matching timestamp format may be incorrectly compared
    end note

    note right of q_api_delete
        INV-005: deletion failures are silently ignored (|| true) to avoid blocking subsequent deletions
        INV-006: each deletion requires correct SHA to prevent race conditions
    end note
